{
  "summary": "The built UI shows many points of alignment with the DESIGN.md – it uses the shared UI primitives, design tokens for spacing, colors and typography, and has solid accessibility scores (axe audit 0 violations, Lighthouse accessibility 98). However the primary user flow is broken: after filling the receipt entry form, the expected \"Receipt saved\" snackbar never appears and navigation back to the dashboard does not happen, causing the acceptance test to time‑out on both phone and desktop. In addition there are a handful of compliance gaps – an undefined `success` color token, decorative icons not hidden from assistive tech, missing focus‑visible styling on buttons, and minor accessibility omissions. These issues must be fixed before the app can be considered polished and production‑ready.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/ReceiptEntryScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The save handler does not display the \"Receipt saved\" Snackbar nor navigate back to the Dashboard after a successful receipt creation, causing the primary flow test to time‑out.",
      "fix": "After the receipt is persisted, call a Snackbar component (or context) with the message \"Receipt saved\", announce it for accessibility, and programmatically navigate back to the Dashboard screen. Ensure the Save button is enabled only when the form is valid and set its loading state appropriately."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/components/ui/SummaryCard.tsx",
      "issue": "The component references `theme.colors.success` for the positive tone, but the theme does not define a `success` color token, resulting in an undefined color style.",
      "fix": "Add a `success` color (e.g., a green value) to the `colors` object in `src/theme.ts` and mirror it in `public/theme.css`. Update the token list and ensure the component uses the new token."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/navigation/index.tsx",
      "issue": "Bottom tab navigation is not guaranteed to be present on all primary screens (e.g., Settings, Export, Backup), violating the spec that the tab bar should be accessible from any screen.",
      "fix": "Wrap each top‑level screen in a BottomTabNavigator (or use a persistent TabBar component) so that the tab bar remains visible and functional across the entire app. Verify that each route is reachable via the tab bar."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/EmptyState.tsx",
      "issue": "The decorative icon (`Avatar.Icon`) is not marked `aria-hidden`, which can cause screen readers to announce it unnecessarily and might trigger axe warnings on stricter audits.",
      "fix": "Add `aria-hidden={true}` (or `aria-hidden`) to the `Avatar.Icon` component to hide it from assistive technology."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Button focus‑visible styling is missing; on web the button does not show the required 2 dp outline when focused, failing the visible focus requirement.",
      "fix": "Add a focus style (e.g., `borderWidth: 2, borderColor: theme.colors.outline`) that is applied when the button receives focus. For React Native Paper, pass a `style` prop that includes a conditional outline based on the `focused` state, or use the `onFocus`/`onBlur` events to toggle a style."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/FormField.tsx",
      "issue": "Error `HelperText` does not have an `aria-live` attribute, so error messages may not be announced immediately by screen readers.",
      "fix": "Wrap the `HelperText` component with `<View aria-live=\"assertive\">` or set the `accessibilityLiveRegion=\"assertive\"` prop on the `HelperText` when `type=\"error\"`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/SettingSwitch.tsx",
      "issue": "Custom switch implementation does not use the native `Switch` component, which may miss platform‑specific accessibility features (e.g., proper `accessibilityRole` handling on iOS/Android).",
      "fix": "Replace the custom track/thumb implementation with React Native Paper's `Switch` component (or React Native's `Switch`) and style it to match the secondary color token. Ensure the `accessibilityLabel` and `value` props are correctly passed."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/ChoiceField.tsx",
      "issue": "The label uses a `Text` component with `accessibilityRole=\"text\"`, which is unnecessary and may not be announced as a label for the segmented buttons.",
      "fix": "Change the label to a `<Text>` with `accessibilityRole=\"heading\"` or simply omit the role, relying on the native association between the label and the `SegmentedButtons`. Ensure the label is programmatically linked if needed."
    }
  ]
}

