{
  "summary": "Overall the app follows the design spec and passes basic Axe and Lighthouse checks, but the primary user flow (saving a receipt) is broken and a few design‑token mismatches cause visual and runtime errors. The most critical issues prevent the core \"add entry\" flow from completing and could surface as crashes or missing UI feedback. Secondary issues are missing accessibility refinements and a stray theme reference (`theme.colors.success`).",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/ReceiptEntryScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "After a successful save the UI never shows the \"Receipt saved\" snackbar and does not navigate back to the Dashboard, causing the acceptance test to time‑out at step 15.",
      "fix": "In the receipt‑save handler, after the store operation succeeds, call `announceForAccessibility('Receipt saved')`, set a state flag that renders `<Snackbar visible={true} onDismiss={...}>Receipt saved</Snackbar>`, and then programmatically navigate to the Dashboard (e.g. using `navigation.navigate('Dashboard')`). Ensure the Snackbar component is part of the render tree and that the `loading` prop on the save button is cleared."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/components/ui/SummaryCard.tsx",
      "issue": "`theme.colors.success` is referenced for the \"positive\" tone, but the theme definition does not include a `success` color token, leading to `undefined` CSS values or runtime errors.",
      "fix": "Add a `success` entry to `theme.colors` (e.g. a green shade that meets contrast) in `src/theme.ts`, or replace the reference with an existing token such as `theme.colors.primary` or a new custom token `colorPositive`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/EmptyState.tsx",
      "issue": "The decorative icon (`<Avatar.Icon>`) lacks `aria-hidden`/`accessible={false}`, so screen readers may announce the icon name, violating the spec that icons are decorative.",
      "fix": "Add `accessibilityIgnoresInvertColors` or `accessible={false}` and `aria-hidden` to the `Avatar.Icon` component, e.g. `<Avatar.Icon ... aria-hidden accessible={false} />`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "No visible focus indicator is applied when the button receives keyboard focus, which is required by the accessibility spec (2 dp outline using `theme.colors.outline`).",
      "fix": "Wrap the Paper `Button` in a `Pressable` or use the `Button`'s `style` prop to add a conditional `outlineWidth: 2, outlineColor: theme.colors.outline` when `focused` (use `onFocus`/`onBlur` to toggle a state) or use the `react-native-paper` `Button`’s `rippleColor` and `mode=\"contained\"` with `theme={...}` that defines `roundness` and `borderWidth` for focus."
