{
  "summary": "Overall the implementation follows the DESIGN.md very closely – screens, state names, copy, spacing and colour tokens are used throughout, components wrap React‑Native‑Paper primitives, and Axe reports zero accessibility violations. The biggest regression is the Export flow: the UI never shows the \"Export ready to share\" snackbar (causing the acceptance test to timeout) and does not handle the error state defined in the spec. A few secondary issues also drift from the spec: the SummaryCard references a non‑existent `theme.colors.success`, the FAB implementation does not match the “primary FAB expands to two mini‑FABs” pattern, some focus‑visible styles are missing, and a few components lack explicit screen‑reader labelling or autocomplete attributes.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/ExportScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The export screen never renders the success snackbar (\"Export ready to share\") and does not have an error snackbar, so the acceptance test step 51 times out and the error state defined in the spec is unimplemented.",
      "fix": "Add state handling for `exportSuccess` and `exportError`. After the native share sheet resolves, set `exportSuccess` true and render a `<Snackbar visible={exportSuccess} onDismiss={() => setExportSuccess(false)}>Export ready to share.</Snackbar>`. Similarly catch errors and show `<Snackbar>` with the error copy. Ensure the snackbar uses the error color token and announces its message for accessibility."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/components/ui/SummaryCard.tsx",
      "issue": "`theme.colors.success` is referenced but the design tokens do not define a `success` colour, causing a runtime undefined colour and breaking the \"positive\" tone variant.",
      "fix": "Add a `success` colour to `src/theme.ts` (e.g. `success: '#006B1F'` and `onSuccess: '#FFFFFF'`) and to `public/theme.css`. Update the colour reference in SummaryCard to use `theme.colors.success` only after the token exists, or replace with an existing token like `primary` if a separate success colour is not required."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/FABAdd.tsx",
      "issue": "Implementation shows two always‑visible mini FABs rather than a primary FAB that expands on press, diverging from the spec’s interaction model and touch‑target sizes.",
      "fix": "Replace the current layout with a single `<FAB size=\"large\" icon=\"plus\" …>` that toggles a local `expanded` state. When expanded, render the two mini FABs (`size=\"small\"`, `mode=\"secondary\"`) positioned 16 dp from the bottom/right. Ensure the primary FAB respects the 56×56 dp target and the mini FABs use the secondary colour background with white icons."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/ChoiceField.tsx",
      "issue": "The label text for the segmented button is not linked to the button group for assistive technologies, so screen‑reader users may not hear the field’s purpose.",
      "fix": "Wrap the `<SegmentedButtons>` in a `<View accessibilityRole=\"radiogroup\" accessibilityLabel={label}>` (or set `accessibilityLabel` directly on `<SegmentedButtons>`). Remove the separate `<Text>` label or set `aria-hidden` on it to avoid duplication."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "No visible focus outline is applied for keyboard navigation on web; the design requires a 2 dp outline using `theme.colors.outline` when the button receives focus.",
      "fix": "Add a `style` prop that includes `borderWidth: 2, borderColor: theme.colors.outline` when the button is focused. Use `onFocus`/`onBlur` to toggle a `focused` state, or rely on CSS `:focus-visible` via `StyleSheet` for web (`...style, { ':focus-visible': { borderWidth: 2, borderColor: theme.colors.outline } }`)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/FormField.tsx",
      "issue": "Form fields do not specify `autoComplete` or appropriate `keyboardType` (e.g., numeric for amount, date picker for date), which can hinder usability and accessibility.",
      "fix": "Pass through `autoComplete` and `keyboardType` props from the parent screen. For amount fields use `keyboardType=\"numeric\"` and `autoComplete=\"off\"`; for date fields use a date picker component with proper accessibility labels."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/EmptyState.tsx",
      "issue": "Prop naming (`body`) does not match the spec (`description`). This could cause copy mismatches if the component is used with the wrong prop name.",
      "fix": "Rename the `body` prop to `description` (and update the component signature and calls) so it aligns with the spec. Keep `body` as an alias if needed for backward compatibility."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/ReceiptCard.tsx",
      "issue": "Placeholder text for attached photo (`[photo attached]`) is hard‑coded and not styled using the design token for secondary text (`theme.colors.onSurfaceVariant`).",
      "fix": "Replace the placeholder text with a `<Text variant=\"bodySmall\" style={{ color: theme.colors.onSurfaceVariant }}>Photo attached</Text>` to respect the token and ensure proper colour contrast."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/SettingSwitch.tsx",
      "issue": "Switch component is not shown, but if it uses the default Paper switch it may render the track in the primary colour instead of the secondary colour required by the spec.",
      "fix": "Override the switch colours: `<Switch trackColor={{ false: theme.colors.surfaceVariant, true: theme.colors.secondary }} thumbColor={value ? theme.colors.onSecondary : theme.colors.onSurfaceVariant} />`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/CheckboxField.tsx",
      "issue": "The `Pressable` wrapper uses a custom `role=\"checkbox\"` but does not set `accessibilityState={{ checked }}` consistently across platforms (only on web?).",
      "fix": "Ensure `accessibilityState={{ checked }}` is set for both iOS and Android as well as web. Also add `accessibilityRole=\"checkbox\"` and `accessibilityHint` if needed."
    }
  ]
}

