{
  "summary": "The project passes basic accessibility (axe 0 violations) and most best‑practice checks (Lighthouse accessibility 98, best‑practices 100) and the UI renders without overflow. However the implementation diverges from the DESIGN.md spec in several critical ways that break the primary user flow and leave required UI states unimplemented. The backup flow never displays the \"Backup ready to share\" snackbar, the FAB does not follow the specified large‑plus‑button‑expand‑to‑mini‑FAB pattern, and several screens lack the loading/error/empty states and copy mandated by the spec. A handful of required components (Delete‑All‑Data confirmation dialog, error views for Dashboard/Receipts/Mileage/Settings) are missing entirely. These gaps are high‑severity because they prevent the user from completing the core flow and constitute accessibility regressions (missing focus‑visible outlines, missing ARIA landmarks on some dialogs). The code also contains a few medium‑severity issues such as hard‑coded colors/sizes, missing autocomplete attributes, and lack of a show/hide toggle for secure passphrase inputs.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/BackupScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "After creating a backup the UI never shows the success Snackbar with the exact text \"Backup ready to share.\" The flow test times out waiting for this message.",
      "fix": "In the backup completion handler, call `showSnackbar('Backup ready to share.')` before opening the share sheet, and ensure the Snackbar component is rendered with the correct message and duration."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/BackupPassphraseScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The passphrase modal does not surface field‑level validation errors (e.g. mismatched or too short passphrases) via `HelperText` and does not focus the first invalid field.",
      "fix": "Add validation logic that sets an `error` prop on `FormField` components, display `HelperText type=\"error\"` with the spec copy, and `ref.focus()` the first failing input. Also disable the \"Create backup\" button until validation passes."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/components/ui/FABAdd.tsx",
      "issue": "The FAB implementation does not match the spec: it renders two always‑visible small FABs instead of a single 56×56 primary FAB that expands to two 40×40 mini‑FABs on press, and it lacks the required 16 dp inset positioning and ripple/focus states.",
      "fix": "Replace the two always‑visible FABs with a single `FAB` (`size=\"large\"`, icon=\"plus\") that toggles a visible state for two `MiniFAB` components. Position the container with `bottom: 16, right: 16`, apply the correct sizes, and add focus‑visible styling (`outline: 2px solid ${theme.colors.outline}`)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The Dashboard screen does not implement the \"Error\" state UI (full‑screen error view with a Retry button and the copy \"Failed to load data. Pull down to retry.\").",
      "fix": "Add a conditional render for an error state that shows a centered view with the error message and a `PrimaryButton` labeled \"Retry\" that triggers data reload."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/ReceiptsScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Missing the full‑screen error view defined in the spec (\"Could not fetch receipts. Pull to retry.\") and the accompanying Retry button.",
      "fix": "Implement an error UI similar to DashboardScreen, using the exact copy and a button that re‑fetches receipts."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/MileageScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Missing the error state UI for mileage loading errors (copy text not rendered).",
      "fix": "Add an error view with the specified copy and a Retry button that re‑loads mileage entries."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/SettingsScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "No Snackbar is displayed when loading settings fails (copy: \"Unable to load settings.\") and the screen lacks proper ARIA role=\"navigation\" for the settings list.",
      "fix": "Wrap the settings list in a `<nav aria-label=\"Settings\">` element (or set `accessibilityRole=\"navigation\"` on the container) and render a `Snackbar` with the error message on load failure."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/components/ui/DeleteAllDataConfirmation.tsx",
      "issue": "The Delete‑All‑Data confirmation dialog component does not exist, despite being required by the spec (title, description, Cancel/Delete buttons, activity indicator during deletion, success Snackbar).",
      "fix": "Create a new component `DeleteAllDataConfirmation` using `Portal`+`Dialog` from React‑Native‑Paper, implement the UI per spec, and expose it for use in SettingsScreen."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/FormField.tsx",
      "issue": "FormField does not forward `autoComplete` or `keyboardType` values for web autocomplete, nor does it expose a toggle for showing/hiding secure text (passphrase fields).",
      "fix": "Accept an optional `autoComplete` prop and pass it to `TextInput`. For secure fields, add an icon button that toggles `secureTextEntry` and updates the label accordingly."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Button focus‑visible style is not defined; on web the default Paper button may not show a visible 2 dp outline as required.",
      "fix": "Add a `style` prop that applies `outline: 2px solid ${theme.colors.outline}` when `focused` (use `onFocus`/`onBlur` state) and ensure the outline is visible in web builds."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/ChoiceField.tsx",
      "issue": "SegmentedButtons do not have an explicit `accessibilityRole=\"radiogroup\"` and each button lacks `role=\"radio\"`, which reduces screen‑reader clarity.",
      "fix": "Wrap the `SegmentedButtons` in a `View` with `accessibilityRole=\"radiogroup\"` and provide `accessibilityRole=\"radio\"` on each button via the `buttons` prop (e.g., `accessibilityState={{ selected: value === o.value }}`)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/EmptyState.tsx",
      "issue": "The `icon` prop is passed to `Avatar.Icon` directly without `aria-hidden`, potentially causing an accessibility reading of decorative icons.",
      "fix": "Add `aria-hidden` to the `Avatar.Icon` component (e.g., `<Avatar.Icon ... aria-hidden />`)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/theme.ts",
      "issue": "Design token `spacing` is exported as a number (8) but used via a custom `space()` helper that may return raw numbers; any direct numeric literals (e.g., `marginBottom: 16`) elsewhere bypass the token system.",
      "fix": "Replace all hard‑coded numeric spacing values with calls to `space(n)` (or equivalent) and ensure `layout` exports a `spacing` function to enforce token usage."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/CheckboxField.tsx",
      "issue": "The component uses `Pressable` with a `style` that does not guarantee a 44×44 dp touch target (gap and padding may be insufficient on small screens).",
      "fix": "Wrap the icon and label in a container with `minHeight: layout.touchTarget` and `minWidth: layout.touchTarget` to enforce the required touch area."
    }
  ]
}

