{
  "summary": "The codebase largely follows the DESIGN.md spec, but there are critical gaps that break the primary user flow and leave some required states and accessibility details unimplemented. The most urgent issue is the backup flow – the \"Backup ready to share\" snackbar never appears, causing the automated UI flow to time‑out. Several screens are missing or incomplete (policy, loading/error states, empty states, validation helpers, and success feedback). Design tokens are used in many components, but a few UI elements still rely on hard‑coded values or miss the required focus‑visible outline. Navigation is mostly wired, yet some primary actions (e.g., the Export screen’s \"Export CSV\"/\"Export PDF\" buttons, the Delete All Data confirmation) are not reachable from every signed‑in screen. Finally, certain components (PrimaryButton, SummaryCard, ReceiptCard, etc.) are not visible in the repository, so we cannot verify that they apply the theme, enforce touch‑target sizes, or expose proper ARIA attributes.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/BackupPassphraseScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The success snackbar with message \"Backup ready to share\" is never rendered after creating a backup, causing the primary UI flow test to fail at step 61.",
      "fix": "Ensure the backup creation promise resolves and triggers a visible <Snackbar> (or calls a showSnackbar utility) with the exact text \"Backup ready to share\". Confirm the Snackbar is mounted in the component tree and not hidden behind a modal or unmounted prematurely."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/PolicyScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Missing loading and error states for the policy gate; only the default acceptance screen is implemented. The spec requires a full‑screen ActivityIndicator with \"Checking policy version…\" and an error view with a Retry button showing \"Unable to store your acceptance. Please try again.\"",
      "fix": "Add a loading state that displays <ActivityIndicator accessibilityLabel=\"Checking policy version…\"/> and an error state that renders a view with the required copy and a Retry button that re‑attempts storing acceptance."
