{
  "summary": "Overall the codebase follows the design system and passes automated accessibility checks, but several critical UI mismatches break core user flows and deviate from the DESIGN.md specifications. The most serious problem is the broken restore‑file chooser, which prevents users from restoring encrypted backups. The policy gate lacks the required error and loading copy states, and the FAB implementation does not match the spec’s expandable primary FAB. Additional medium‑severity issues include mismatched EmptyState props, missing focus‑visible outlines on buttons, touch‑target size violations, and layout constraints not enforced on the generic Screen component. These gaps must be fixed before the app can be considered a polished product.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/RestoreScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The \"Select backup file\" button never opens the file chooser; the UI flow test timed‑out waiting for a \"filechooser\" event, so users cannot restore backups.",
      "fix": "Wrap the button in a native `<input type=\"file\">` element for the web (or use `expo-document-picker` with `await DocumentPicker.getDocumentAsync()` and ensure the click handler is attached to the button). Export the element’s `onPress` to trigger `DocumentPicker.launchAsync`. Add a fallback for non‑native platforms and verify the button has `accessibilityLabel=\"Select backup file\"` and `role=\"button\"`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/PolicyScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Missing UI for the PolicyGateScreen error state (no \"Retry\" button) and the loading state does not display the required copy \"Checking policy version…\"; only a generic ActivityIndicator is shown.",
      "fix": "Add three distinct render branches: (1) Loading – show `<ActivityIndicator size=\"large\" />` with a `<Text>` containing \"Checking policy version…\"; (2) Default – display policy text, checkbox, and disabled Accept button; (3) Error – render a full‑screen error view with the message \"Unable to store your acceptance. Please try again.\" and a PrimaryButton labeled \"Retry\" that re‑invokes the acceptance storage logic."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/components/ui/FABAdd.tsx",
      "issue": "Implementation diverges from the spec: two always‑visible mini‑FABs are rendered instead of a single large FAB that expands to show the receipt and mileage mini‑FABs on press. This also violates the required touch‑target size (mini‑FABs are 40 × 40 dp, below the 44 × 44 dp minimum for interactive elements).",
      "fix": "Refactor FABAdd to render a single large `<FAB size=\"large\" icon=\"plus\" …>` that toggles an internal `expanded` state. When expanded, render the two mini‑FABs (`size=\"small\"`) inside a `Portal` with proper spacing. Ensure mini‑FABs are wrapped in a `Pressable` that adds extra invisible padding to meet the 44 dp touch target requirement, and style them with `backgroundColor: theme.colors.secondary` per the design tokens."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/EmptyState.tsx",
      "issue": "Prop naming does not align with the spec (`body` instead of `description`). The component also forwards `label` to `PrimaryButton` which may expect children text, risking missing button label styling.",
      "fix": "Rename the `body` prop to `description` (or accept both) and pass the text to `PrimaryButton` as `children` (or via a `label` prop that `PrimaryButton` supports). Update all callers to use the new prop name and add a default prop to maintain backward compatibility."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "The button wrapper does not appear to implement the required focus‑visible outline (2 dp using `theme.colors.outline`) and may omit hover/active visual states on web.",
      "fix": "Add a style that applies `outlineWidth: 2`, `outlineColor: theme.colors.outline`, and `outlineStyle: 'solid'` when the button receives `focusVisible` (use `Pressable`’s `onFocus`/`onBlur` or React Native Web's `:focus-visible`). Ensure hover (`onMouseEnter`) and active (`onPressIn`) states adjust elevation or background per spec."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/ExportButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Uses hard‑coded numeric margin (`marginVertical: 8`) instead of the 8 dp grid token (`space(1)`). This may cause inconsistent spacing across the app.",
      "fix": "Replace the literal `8` with `space(1)` (or `theme.spacing * 1`) and confirm the vertical rhythm aligns with the rest of the UI."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/Screen.tsx",
      "issue": "The generic `Screen` component does not enforce the design system’s horizontal padding of 16 dp, the max content width of 420 dp, or the mobile‑first layout constraints described in DESIGN.md.",
      "fix": "Wrap children in a `<View style={{ paddingHorizontal: space(2), maxWidth: 420, alignSelf: 'center', width: '100%' }}>` ensuring the layout respects the 16 dp padding and 420 dp max width. Verify that the component works unchanged on larger viewports (desktop breakpoint)."
