{
  "summary": "The app generally follows the design system, tokens, and accessibility guidelines, but the primary user flow is broken because the restore screen never opens the native file picker. A handful of UI implementations also diverge from the spec (FAB layout, hard‑coded spacing, missing focus outlines, mini‑FAB touch‑area size, and a few copy mismatches). Fixing the file‑chooser bug restores the critical backup‑restore flow; the remaining issues are cosmetic or accessibility improvements.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/RestoreScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The \"Select backup file\" button does not trigger a file chooser on web or in the Playwright test, causing the primary backup‑restore flow to time‑out on both phone and desktop viewports.",
      "fix": "Implement a web‑compatible file picker. For the web, render a hidden `<input type=\"file\" accept=\"*/*\" />` and forward its click from the button, then handle the `onChange` event to read the selected file. Ensure the same handler is used for expo‑document‑picker on native platforms. Add an `aria‑label` and `role=\"button\"` to the visible button for accessibility."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/FABAdd.tsx",
      "issue": "The design calls for a single large FAB that expands to two mini‑FABs, but the implementation always shows two small FABs side‑by‑side, deviating from the spec and missing the primary FAB's affordance.",
      "fix": "Replace the two always‑visible FABs with a single large FAB (`size=\"large\"`) that toggles a state (`showMini`) on press. Render the two mini‑FABs (`size=\"small\"`) conditionally within a `Portal` when `showMini` is true. Ensure the mini‑FABs retain the required 40 dp size and add a 2 dp focus outline for web."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/ExportButton.tsx",
      "issue": "The button uses a hard‑coded `marginVertical: 8` value, bypassing the design token `spacing` (8 dp base unit). This creates inconsistency with other components that use the `space()` utility.",
      "fix": "Replace the hard‑coded margin with `style={{ marginVertical: space(1), backgroundColor: theme.colors.secondary }}` (import `space` from `../../theme`)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "The component receives a `label` prop but it is unclear whether it forwards this to the underlying Paper `Button` as its child text. If the prop is ignored, the button may render without visible text, breaking UI expectations for labels such as \"Add receipt\" or \"Create backup\".",
      "fix": "Ensure `PrimaryButton` renders the button label either via `{children}` or by passing the `label` prop to the `Button`'s children. Example: `<Button {...props}>{label}</Button>`. Add a PropTypes or TypeScript definition that makes `label` required."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/PolicyScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The error view copy does not match the spec: the design requires the message \"Unable to store your acceptance. Please try again.\" but the implementation may use different wording.",
      "fix": "Update the error view's `Text` component to display the exact copy from DESIGN.md. Verify the Retry button is present and disabled state is handled correctly."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The empty‑state primary action button label should be exactly \"Add receipt\" (title‑case). If the button text differs (e.g., \"Add Receipt\" or \"Add\"), it violates the copy spec and may affect UI tests.",
      "fix": "Set the button's `label` or `children` to the literal string \"Add receipt\". Keep the button case‑consistent with other labels."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/EmptyState.tsx",
      "issue": "The decorative icon rendered via `Avatar.Icon` lacks an explicit `accessibilityLabel`, which may cause screen readers to announce the icon name unintentionally or omit useful context.",
      "fix": "Add `accessibilityLabel=\"empty state illustration\"` and `accessible={false}` (or `aria-hidden`) to the `Avatar.Icon` to make it truly decorative."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/FormField.tsx",
      "issue": "Form fields for numeric input (amount, miles) do not set `keyboardType=\"numeric\"` or `autoComplete` attributes, missing an opportunity for better UX and accessibility.",
      "fix": "When using `FormField` for numeric fields, spread `keyboardType=\"numeric\"` and `autoComplete=\"off\"` (or appropriate type) into the component. Adjust the component's PropTypes to allow these props."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Focus‑visible styling is not implemented; on web the button does not show the required 2 dp outline when focused via keyboard.",
      "fix": "Add a `:focus-visible` style (or use `onFocus`/`onBlur` state) that applies `borderWidth: 2, borderColor: theme.colors.outline` to the button container."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/MiniFAB.tsx (rendered inside FABAdd)",
      "issue": "Mini‑FAB size is 40 dp, which is below the required minimum touch target of 44 × 44 dp per the design guidelines.",
      "fix": "Wrap each mini‑FAB in a `Pressable` with a transparent hit‑area of at least 44 dp (e.g., using `padding: 2` around the FAB) or increase the FAB size to 44 dp while keeping the visual icon at 40 dp."
    }
  ]
}

